{"name":"Strong Winds","hex":"#a3a59b","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"strong","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Capable of producing great physical force.","Capable of withstanding great physical force."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Strong people, collectively."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strong"},{"term":"winds","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of wind"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of wind"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/winds"}],"entries":[{"title":"Strong Winds","blocks":[{"text":"Strong Winds is a 1924 German silent film directed by Reinhold Schünzel and starring Maria Kamradek, Alwin Neuss and Albert Bennefeld."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d0/Strong_Winds_screenshot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strong_Winds"},{"title":"Beaufort scale","blocks":[{"text":"The Beaufort scale is an empirical measure that relates wind speed to observed conditions at sea or on land. Its full name is the Beaufort wind force scale. It was devised in 1805 by Francis Beaufort, a hydrographer in the British Royal Navy. It was officially adopted by the Royal Navy and later spread internationally."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Beaufort_scale_12_notext.jpg/330px-Beaufort_scale_12_notext.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beaufort_scale"},{"title":"Wind","blocks":[{"text":"Wind is the natural movement of air or other gases relative to a planet's surface. Winds occur on a range of scales, from thunderstorm flows lasting tens of minutes, to local breezes generated by heating of land surfaces and lasting a few hours, to global winds resulting from the difference in absorption of solar energy between the climate zones on Earth. The study of wind is known as anemology."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Cherry_tree_moving_in_the_wind_1.gif/330px-Cherry_tree_moving_in_the_wind_1.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wind"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/FrancisBeaufort.jpg/500px-FrancisBeaufort.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/FrancisBeaufort.jpg/500px-FrancisBeaufort.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sir Francis Beaufort","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFrancisBeaufort.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Beaufort_wind_scale.png/500px-Beaufort_wind_scale.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Beaufort_wind_scale.png/500px-Beaufort_wind_scale.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Data graphic showing Beaufort wind force in scale units, knots and metres per second","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABeaufort_wind_scale.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Beaufort_scale_0.jpg/330px-Beaufort_scale_0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Beaufort_scale_0.jpg/330px-Beaufort_scale_0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABeaufort_scale_0.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Beaufort_scale_1.jpg/330px-Beaufort_scale_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://